---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import fs from "fs";
import path from "path";
import { fileURLToPath } from "url";
import EditorialStandardsCard from "../../components/EditorialStandardsCard.astro";

interface BlogPost {
  title: string;
  description: string;
  slug: string;
  date: string;
  readTime: string;
  author: string;
}

const posts: BlogPost[] = [];
const currentDir = path.resolve(process.cwd(), 'src/pages/blogs');

if (fs.existsSync(currentDir)) {
  const files = fs.readdirSync(currentDir).filter(f => f.endsWith('.astro') && f !== 'index.astro');
  for (const file of files) {
    const filePath = path.join(currentDir, file);
    const content = fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8');

    const titleMatch = content.match(/const title = ["']([^"']+)["']/);
    const descMatch = content.match(/const description = ["']([^"']+)["']/);
    const dateMatch = content.match(/Last updated: ([^|]+)/) || content.match(/const lastUpdated = ["']([^"']+)["']/);
    const readTimeMatch = content.match(/(\d+) min read/);
    const authorMatch = content.match(/const author = ["']([^"']+)["']/);

    if (titleMatch && descMatch) {
      posts.push({
        title: titleMatch[1],
        description: descMatch[1],
        slug: `/blogs/${file.replace(/\.astro$/, '')}`,
        date: dateMatch ? (dateMatch[1] ? dateMatch[1].trim() : 'July 2026') : 'July 2026',
        readTime: readTimeMatch ? `${readTimeMatch[1]} min read` : '10 min read',
        author: authorMatch ? authorMatch[1] : 'Finsiva Research & Methodology'
      });
    }
  }
}

posts.sort((a, b) => a.title.localeCompare(b.title));
---

<Layout title="Tax Blog - Latest Tax Tips, Guides & Updates | TaxPortal" description="Read the latest tax tips, guides, and updates from TaxPortal. Learn about income tax, GST, TDS, capital gains, and tax saving strategies.">
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-canvas dark:bg-canvas">
    <main class="min-h-screen">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-ink mb-8 dark:text-on-primary">Tax Blog</h1>
        <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1556761175-5973dc0f32e7?w=1200&q=80" alt="Tax blog header with financial news" class="mb-6 w-full rounded-lg object-cover max-h-80 sm:max-h-96" loading="lazy" />
        <p class="text-lg text-body dark:text-muted mb-12">Latest tax tips, guides, and updates to help you stay informed and save taxes.</p>
        
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          {posts.map(post => (
            <article class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 transition hover:border-primary hover:shadow-lg dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface dark:hover:border-primary">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-2 dark:text-on-primary">
                <a href={post.slug} class="hover:text-primary dark:hover:text-link">{post.title}</a>
              </h2>
              <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-4 dark:text-muted">{post.description}</p>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted">
                <span>By {post.author}</span>
                <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                <span>{post.date}</span>
                <span>{post.readTime}</span>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6 dark:border-overlay-light dark:bg-surface">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-3 dark:text-on-primary">About Our Blog</h2>
          <p class="text-body dark:text-muted">TaxPortal's blog features expert analysis from tax professionals and financial analysts. Our team of contributors includes Maya Lin (US tax), Kira Tanaka (India GST/TDS), Nora Chen (capital gains), Hana Patel (TDS deductions), Lena Park (Indian tax calculations), and Sora Vance (old vs new tax regimes). Browse our guides for actionable tax strategies and calculators for every tax scenario.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-body dark:text-muted">Every article follows a strict editorial process: initial research against official government sources, professional review by at least one qualified contributor, fact-checking before publication, and a post-publication review cycle when tax laws change. We clearly mark content as informational and encourage readers to consult a tax professional for personalized advice.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-body dark:text-muted">Our blog covers a wide range of topics, from basic tax filing tips to advanced strategies for investors and business owners. We publish new articles weekly, with special focus on tax season deadlines, budget announcements, and regulatory updates that affect our supported countries.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-body dark:text-muted">Whether you are filing your first tax return or managing a portfolio of international investments, our blog provides context and clarity that generic financial news often lacks. We explain not just what changed, but why it changed and how it affects real people.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-body dark:text-muted"><a href="/about/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Learn more about our team</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <EditorialStandardsCard class="mt-12" />

        <div class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6 dark:border-overlay-light dark:bg-surface">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink mb-3 dark:text-on-primary">Newsletter Signup</h2>
          <p class="text-body dark:text-muted mb-4">Stay up to date with the latest tax tips, calculator releases, and policy changes. Our newsletter is sent once a month and includes curated articles, upcoming deadline reminders, and exclusive guides for our subscribers.</p>
          <form action="https://formspree.io/f/xpqvelrz" method="POST" class="space-y-4">
            <div>
              <label for="newsletter-email" class="block text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1 dark:text-on-primary">Email address</label>
              <input type="email" id="newsletter-email" name="email" required class="w-full rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas px-4 py-2 text-ink focus:border-primary focus:outline-none dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface dark:text-on-primary" />
            </div>
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Subscribe</button>
          </form>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted dark:text-muted">We respect your privacy. Unsubscribe at any time. No spam, ever.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<div class="mt-12 space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">The Psychology Behind Navigating your tax obligations</h2>
  <p>
    Let's be incredibly honest for a moment. When you're trying to understand <strong>your tax obligations</strong>, the sheer volume of bureaucratic jargon can feel entirely overwhelming. It’s not just about the numbers or the compliance—it's about the psychological weight of getting it right. Fear of penalties, the stress of audits, and the anxiety of misinterpreting complex regulations are universal pain points.
  </p>
  <p>
    Many taxpayers and business owners experience what financial psychologists call "compliance fatigue." You are expected to be an expert in everything from withholding rules to obscure deduction clauses. The truth is, mastering your tax obligations requires a shift in mindset: from reactive compliance to proactive wealth preservation.
  </p>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-6">Advanced Strategies for Minimizing Risk</h3>
  <p>
    Beyond the basic rules, the most successful individuals and corporations employ advanced, legally sound strategies. Here is how you can move from surviving to thriving:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mt-4">
    <li><strong>Documentation is Your Shield:</strong> Never rely on memory. Maintain granular, digitized records of all expenses, receipts, and correspondence. A well-organized ledger is your best defense against arbitrary assessments.</li>
    <li><strong>Strategic Timing:</strong> The timing of income recognition and expense realization can drastically alter your tax footprint. Accelerating deductions or deferring income into the next fiscal period is a cornerstone of intelligent planning.</li>
    <li><strong>Professional Consultation over DIY:</strong> The cost of an expert is almost always lower than the cost of a compliance error. Navigating your tax obligations without professional counsel is an unnecessary risk.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-6">Troubleshooting Common Edge-Case Scenarios</h3>
  <p>
    What happens when things don't go according to plan? Let's address some edge cases that frequently trip up even seasoned professionals when dealing with your tax obligations:
  </p>
  <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 mt-4">
    <li><strong>Discrepancies in Source Documents:</strong> If a withholding certificate or an income statement contains errors, do not adjust your return to match the error. Request a formal correction from the issuer immediately.</li>
    <li><strong>Multi-Jurisdictional Conflicts:</strong> If your income crosses borders, you may face double taxation. Always invoke the relevant Double Taxation Avoidance Agreements (DTAA) and ensure you have the necessary tax residency certificates on hand.</li>
    <li><strong>Late Filing Repercussions:</strong> If you miss a deadline, the worst action is inaction. File as soon as possible and proactively request a waiver of penalties citing reasonable cause, if applicable.</li>
  </ol>

  <p class="mt-6 font-medium">
    Ultimately, navigating these regulations is a marathon, not a sprint. By prioritizing structured planning and mental clarity, you can turn a compliance burden into a strategic advantage.
  </p>
</div>
